{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_e58887681b1bb36895a04abe30e4c5fd6e16f4d03e0e2f7dbb54c1c58c416fa9", "title": "Hotel Rwanda", "text": "Hotel Rwanda is a 2004 British-Italian-South African historical drama film directed by Terry George. It was adapted from a screenplay written by both George and Keir Pearson. It stars Don Cheadle and Sophie Okonedo as hotelier Paul Rusesabagina and his wife Tatiana. Based on the Rwandan genocide, which occurred during the spring of 1994, the film, which has been called an African \"Schindler's List\", documents Rusesabagina's acts to save the lives of his family and more than a thousand other refugees by providing them with shelter in the besieged Hôtel des Mille Collines. \"Hotel Rwanda\" explores genocide, political corruption, and the repercussions of violence.", "score": 32.9679}, {"id": "hp_doc_f660354b99ffb8d66310fe15cfd442bfc08865d7284943abea73d411f75daa2c", "title": "Leleti Khumalo", "text": "Leleti Khumalo (born 1970) is a Zulu South African actress known for her leading role in the movie and stage play \"Sarafina! \" and for her roles in other films such as \"Hotel Rwanda\", \"Yesterday\" and \"Invictus\".", "score": 16.6958}, {"id": "hp_doc_58cd71dec9c665e8f11eff4c6dd90af5944f3a54b69c3f0b0dd2ec36fe13d757", "title": "Temoer Terry", "text": "Temoer Terry (born June 12, 1975 in McPherson, Kansas) is a former college wrestling champion. Wrestling out of the University of Nebraska, (1994–1998), he had a collegiate record of 100-24. Terry had a record of 79-3 at McPherson High School. Terry has also coached at the college level for American University. Also coached for George Mason University", "score": 14.7255}], "remaining_searches": 1}
